]. Low-molecular-weight fucoidan (LMWF) with a unique structure obtained from Japanese kelp can inhibit the phosphorylation of PI3K and Akt, downregulate the PI3K/AKT signaling pathway, and inhibit the progression of EMT [
160
]. Moreover, the STAT3 cascade is another pivotal pathway driving pulmonary fibrosis [
